[129.155,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your Azure subscription (location northeurope); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: the stack's own key pair, its public half handed to the template (.openvidu/azure/ov-e2ee-s132250-key.pub)\r\n  2. Template: render the elastic template into .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-pro-elastic.bicep\r\n     and its secure parameters into .openvidu/azure/secure-parameters.json (0600)\r\n  3. Machines: Update the deployment ov-e2ee-s132250 with the master and the media nodes: the master installs OpenVidu and the media nodes join it (about 5 minutes)\r\n  4. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on Azure…\r\n"]
[129.846,"o","   · apply the parameters that changed to deployment ov-e2ee-s132250 (incremental: what they do not touch stays; this returns when Azure is done)\r\n"]
